{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler stitch task (#5222) to implement srd008-ls requirements R3.12-R3.15 in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires:\n   - Implementing R3.12: -R must respect the current format mode (long format with total line, multi-column with -C or default)\n   - Implementing R3.13: -R must not follow symbolic links to directories\n   - Implementing R3.14: -R must apply current filter flags (-a, -A) to subdirectories\n   - Implementing R3.15: -R must list directories in the same sort order as entries\n   - Adding differential test cases for each requirement\n   - Verifying with `go build`, `go test`, and `go vet`\n   \n   Git is managed externally - NO git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary `gls` via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `pkg/sys.Lstat` for file metadata without following symlinks\n   - `pkg/format.Columns`, `pkg/format.HumanSize`, `pkg/format.FileTypeColor` for output formatting\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic sort order in tests\n   - The \"last flag wins\" pattern for mutually exclusive options\n   - Recursive directory listing with format-mode preservation\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml** (lines 163-170 are key):\n     - Contains the full specification for R3.12-R3.15\n     - R3.12: \"-R must respect the current format mode. With -l, each subdirectory's contents are listed in long format including the 'total N' block line. With -C or default mode, each subdirectory's contents use multi-column layout.\"\n     - R3.13: \"-R must not follow symbolic links to directories. Only real subdirectories are recursed into.\"\n     - R3.14: \"-R must apply the current filter flags (-a, -A) to each subdirectory. Dotfiles in subdirectories are shown only if -a or -A is given.\"\n     - R3.15: \"-R must list directories in the same sort order as entries within a directory. If -t is active, subdirectories are recursed into in modification-time order.\"\n\n   - **cmd/ls/main.go** (full file, 881 lines):\n     - Already has `recurseSubdirs` function (lines 299-315) that handles recursive listing\n     - Key function: `listDir` (lines 276-297) handles both long format and column format\n     - `readNames` (lines 317-334) applies filter flags and sorting\n     - `sortEntries` (lines 336-391) handles all sort modes\n     - The implementation appears to already satisfy R3.12-R3.15 functionally because:\n       - `listDir` is called for each subdirectory with the same `opts`, preserving format mode (R3.12)\n       - `os.Lstat` is used in `recurseSubdirs` so symlinks aren't followed (R3.13)\n       - `readNames` applies filter flags from `opts` (R3.14)\n       - `names` are already sorted before `recurseSubdirs` iterates them (R3.15)\n\n   - **cmd/ls/ls_test.go** (279 lines):\n     - Uses `testutils.RunDiffTests` pattern with `gls` reference binary\n     - Has helper functions: `setupDir`, `setupTimeSortDir`, `setupSizeSortDir`, `setupHumanSizeDir`, `setupClassifyDir`, `setupRecursiveDir`\n     - Already has tests: \"recursive-flag\" (-1R), \"recursive-long\" (-lR), \"recursive-all\" (-1Ra)\n     - Needs additional tests specifically targeting R3.12 (recursive with -C), R3.13 (symlink to directory not recursed), R3.14 (already partially covered by \"recursive-all\"), R3.15 (recursive with -t sort)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was interrupted after reading files and before implementation.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the core recursive functionality appears already implemented in `recurseSubdirs` and `lis